

### 26.5 Incomplete Beta Function

\(I_{x}(a,b)\!=\!\frac{1}{B(a,b)}\int_{0}^{x}\!\!t^{a-1}(1\!-\!t)^{b-1}dt\)\((0\!\leq\!x\!\leq\!1)\)

\(I_{z}(a,b)\!=\!1\!-\!I_{1-x}(b,a)\)

##### Relation to the Chi-Square Distribution

If \(X_{1}^{2}\) and \(X_{2}^{3}\) are independent random variables following chi-square distributions 26.4.1 with \(r_{1}\) and \(r_{2}\) degrees of freedom respectively, then \(\frac{X_{1}^{2}}{X_{1}^{2}\!+\!X_{2}^{3}}\) is said to follow a beta distribution with \(r_{1}\) and \(r_{2}\) degrees of freedom and has the distribution function

